cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use feynkit in your work, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: feynkit
abstract: >-
  A Python package for Feynman integrals via GKZ systems: Symanzik
  polynomials, parametric representations, the GKZ system, the Newton
  polytope with exact faces, facets and volumes, the toric ideal,
  symmetries, Landau singularities, finite-field point counts that give a
  candidate number of master integrals, and an analysis report.
authors:
  - family-names: Denham
    given-names: Byron
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-09-27"
repository-code: https://github.com/byrondenham/feynkit
url: https://github.com/byrondenham/feynkit
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Feynman integrals
  - GKZ systems
  - A-hypergeometric functions
  - Newton polytopes
  - toric ideals
  - master integrals
  - point counting
